On 30 November 2012 11:33, jongausib <so.cool.ogi@gmail.com> wrote:

> brailyle'u is not a valid lujvo. You can't have a fu'ivla and a gismu as a
> veljvo. In that case you'll have to use "zei".
>

Actually, {braile} being of the form CCVVCV is one of the forms to which
(even) the CLL assigns what it calls a fu'ivla rafsi. Maybe you recall the
example of {tci'ile} that it uses to demonstrate a use-case of this
proposal?

Regardless, as selpa'i mentioned, the PEG gives a rafsi to *every* fu'ivla
(even {.irci}, for example). That being said, we could create a lujvo for
"irc bot" {.irci'yzmi}.

.i mi'e la tsani mu'o

